00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.280
You don't like bread?

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:55.790
It's not that I don't like it, but I prefer rice after all...

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.000
Don't you think so?

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.960
W-Well...

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:01.920
Because this is curry.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.000
Whenever you mention curry, rice follows.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.050
Curry rice, or rice curry.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:09.630
Y-Yeah...

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:15.350
Besides, if you want curry to go with bread,
there's already something called "curry bread."

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:17.600
A-Ana-chan...

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:22.020
Ana-chan, your Japanese has improved.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:26.690
W-What?

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:31.400
It's natural, since she has stayed in Japan for a long time.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.570
I see.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.870
You're right.

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:36.450
Th-That's not true.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:43.880
I'm a genuine British girl, born in Cornwall.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:50.170
Therefore, don’t confuse me with "youtoukuniku," a kind of foreigner who speaks nothing but Japanese…

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:52.840
Ana-chan...

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:55.800
What is "youtoukuniku"?

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:01.060
Let's see... It says, "The appearance doesn't match the content."

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:04.600
Amazing...

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:05.860
Amazing!

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.270
Ah, I see...

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:14.410
I said I didn't want to.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.870
Just press it.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.470
Ah! How come Nobu-neechan is over there?

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.430
From whom?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:04.660
Funga...!

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:21.890
Why me?

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.460
I was really surprised today.

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:49.290
But from now on you can speak Japanese in the classroom.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.420
I-I won't.

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:55.630
I'm starving.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:59.760
If I collapse due to hunger, it would be the mistake of my life.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.600
Oh, this is...

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.430
The tougenkyou that we have been looking for.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.810
Chi-chan, let's go.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:07.060
Do you have any money?

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:10.060
This is tougenkyou! Tougenkyou!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.320
If you want to go, go by yourself.

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:16.110
What’s with you? I won't show you my homework anymore.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.030
Isn't it the opposite?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:17.860
Besides, you've never finished your homework before me, have you?

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.240
Hey.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.780
What is tougenkyou?

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.540
Oh yeah, I should ask Miu-chan.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.580
I can assure you that she doesn't know.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.500
Anyway, I'll pass today.

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:34.210
Chi-chan, you’re stingy!

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:35.420
I'm fine with being stingy.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.050
I've found a rich girl!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.010
I-I'm not rich at all.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.470
Liar! Show me your wallet.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.850
What are you doing?

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.780
Ana-chan, let me be your servant.

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.360
Ah, that's fine.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.030
Are you sure?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.290
I'm going to take these.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.580
Take this one too.

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.750
That's crafty.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.840
Why not? You're rich.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.800
Don't be stingy.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:22.510
That's not what stingy means.

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:25.810
I'm buying things that can be shared with everyone.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.640
I will leave it to you, then.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:29.020
Ah, wait!

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:29.980
Micchan!

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:32.520
I'm leaving the payment here.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:33.480
Miu-san!

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:34.940
Hey!

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:36.520
You shouldn't!

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.280
I already ate them.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:11.270
Slurp

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.570
This is beyond realistic.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:46.390
Micchan, stop already.

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:48.050
Well then, next question.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:52.140
There was a bus carrying ten passengers.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:55.140
At the Takamachi station, three people got off, and one got on.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.610
At the Yurinokidoori station, six people got on.

00:15:57.610 --> 00:15:59.980
Now, how many people are there on the bus?

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.650
I won't be tricked.

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:04.820
There are fifteen people, including the driver.

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:07.110
Should be fourteen people.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:07.950
Why?

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:12.870
Because one of the passengers is a failure as a human being.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.210
Go away.

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:16.370
Eh? Onee-chan is not home?

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.340
<i>Masaka
Park</i>
Eh? Onee-chan is not home?

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:45.440
Tou... Tou... Tougenkyou...

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:46.530
Found it.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:48.360
It means Risoukyou.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.660
Risoukyou?

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.450
Let's see... Risoukyou...

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.080
It means Utopia.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.620
U-Utopia?

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.670
U... U... U...

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:00.590
Utopia.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.460
It means Risoukyou.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:09.180
Well, this is what life is about.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.510
What did you just conclude?

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:23.070
Let's see... Found it.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:26.280
Sen - Ten times of hundred.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:28.740
Seems like it just means what it means.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:32.070
Ka - Exceptionally good thing.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:36.200
It means there are a thousand exceptionally good things, right?

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.120
Yeah.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:39.290
Next one is Matsuri-chan, then.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.500
Ma... Ma... Ma...

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:42.750
I will do it.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.420
Let's see...

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:48.550
Orthoptera. An insect that belongs to the cricket family.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:52.470
Distributed in the south of Honshu. Its chirping sound is "chinchirourin."

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:56.470
Matsumushi.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:57.930
I knew it.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.100
Give me!

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.810
Matsuri... It should be somewhere more ahead...

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.730
Found it. Matsurika.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.240
Matsurika?

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:13.490
Let's see... A plant that belongs to the Oleaceae. A species of Jasmine.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:15.450
J-Jasmine?

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:18.120
It said Jasmine, Matsuri-chan.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:19.410
Nice to meet you, Jasmine.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:22.210
D-Don't call me that.

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.710
But it's kind of enviable.

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:25.710
Really?

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:30.130
Let's see... A spicing plant that originated in India.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:34.470
People in China put its flowers into the tea that becomes Jasmine tea.

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:36.220
Nice to meet you, originated in India.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:39.060
S-Stop it already.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:40.980
Next one is Ana-chan, then.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:41.690
Me?

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:46.520
Ana - A place that's caved in.

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:50.070
Hold on a second! It's not "aNa," it's "Ana."

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:54.530
But that's too bad, since this is the only one.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.500
Ana - A place that's caved in.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.660
A broken, imperfect place.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.580
Weakness. Loss.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.250
Ana - A place that's caved in.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.260
Why are you reading it again?

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:13.010
What a beautiful sunset.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:14.220
You're right.

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:16.010
See you tomorrow.

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:17.890
Yeah. See you.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:19.970
See you, originated in India.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.770
Stop it already.

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:24.980
You will probably be called that for a while.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.610
See you, a place that's caved in.

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:29.440
I'm really going to get angry.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:33.950
Satake

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:45.210
Ah, how calming.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:17.070
Coward. Are you still a man?

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.120
No, I'm not a man.

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:24.660
Oww, oww, oww, it hurts.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.750
Stay still. Just a little bit more.

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:33.590
Oil pen is unexpectedly tough to get off.

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:34.920
That's why I told you.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:41.930
Mom told you to stop that, didn't she?

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:45.890
What's wrong with it? It's not like I'm causing anyone trouble.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:51.020
Enough with it already. It's bad for your health.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:54.190
Where did you learn that from?

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:57.570
It's okay. Mama, let me drink it to the end today.

00:20:57.570 --> 00:20:58.110
Playing double roles?

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:03.240
I'm going to forget about that person.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.330
It's ten years too early for you.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.710
She's completely behaving like an old man.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.710
Nah, already at the retirement age.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:18.800
With his second life already over, right now he is...

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.760
Whatever.

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:25.180
How should I put it...

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:29.900
This is a blessing.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:36.900
Tougenkyou?

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.110
Utopia?

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.180
I will have some milk too.

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:58.780
<b>Pudding
Chika</b>

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:22.680
I can't hear anything from the sky as it turns madder red
nanimo kikoenai sora no iro wa akane

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:32.770
The memories are always soft to the touch
kioku wa itsumo yasashii tezawari

00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:41.940
It gently gives me a smile
sotto hohoemi wo kureru

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:51.870
I flew a paper airplane just now, didn't I?
kamihikouki sakki tobashita deshou

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:59.750
An ephemeral, parabola
hakanasugiru houbutsusen

00:24:00.210 --> 00:24:02.720
It's fluffy
furirura

00:24:02.880 --> 00:24:12.810
Though I've grown up without noticing it
itsunomanika otona ni natte takedo

00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:18.520
I waited for the rain to stop all this time
machibouketa ameagari

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:33.250
The smell after the rain was surprisingly soft
odoroku hodo yasashii nioi ga shiteta

00:24:37.210 --> 00:24:42.210
Always.
Next
